This directory contains the BRLTTY driver for the InsideONE braille display by
InsideVision [http://www.insidevision.fr/].

Unlike the original driver, which was a TCP client of the vendor's Windows Core
daemon, this one talks to the hardware directly over USB HID and needs no vendor
software. It drives two HID devices:

  * the KGS braille module (VID 0x10C4, PID 0x82CD) for the 32 cells, the
    blinking cursor and the sleep/backlight state;
  * the multitouch digitizer for all input.

The digitizer's USB identifiers are not yet hard-coded. Supply them (hex) with
the driver parameters until they are confirmed on hardware, e.g.:

  brltty -b iv -B touchvendor=XXXX,touchproduct=YYYY

With no touch identifiers the braille output still works; input is disabled.
